cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Voicebox in academic work or build on it, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Voicebox: an open-source, local-first AI voice studio"
abstract: >-
  Voicebox is a free and open-source desktop application combining multi-engine
  voice cloning, text-to-speech, system-wide dictation, and agent voice output
  via the Model Context Protocol. All inference runs locally on the user's
  machine (MLX on Apple Silicon; PyTorch on CUDA, ROCm, DirectML, Intel XPU, or
  CPU elsewhere). Ships seven TTS engines (Qwen3-TTS, Qwen CustomVoice, LuxTTS,
  Chatterbox Multilingual, Chatterbox Turbo, HumeAI TADA, Kokoro) plus OpenAI
  Whisper for transcription and a bundled Qwen3 LLM for refinement and personas.
type: software
license: MIT
